 - [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission includes a base_revision that matches the visit's latest resolved revision, the system SHALL accept it as a new revision with revision number = latest resolved revision + 1.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission includes a base_revision that does not match the visit's latest resolved revision, the system SHALL accept it as a competing revision with revision number = latest resolved revision + 1 and mark the visit as having unresolved review work.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When multiple submissions share the same base_revision, the system SHALL preserve all as competing revisions awaiting resolution.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a caller retrieves a visit with competing revisions, the system SHALL return the latest resolved revision (or initial visit if none resolved) as current_payload, set has_unresolved to true, and include all competing revisions in competing_revisions.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a caller retrieves a visit with no competing revisions, the system SHALL return the latest resolved revision as current_payload, set has_unresolved to false, and return an empty competing_revisions array.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a coordinator resolves competing revisions, the system SHALL create a new resolved revision with a revision number one greater than the previous latest resolved revision, store the resolved payload, and record the resolving coordinator's identity, resolution timestamp, contributing revision numbers, and optional resolution note.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a resolution is created, the system SHALL retain all contributing submissions unchanged and queryable by their revision numbers.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When a submission references a visit_id that does not exist, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: When a submission's payload fails field-type validation or references an unknown plot ID, the system SHALL reject the submission.
